    <!--
        THIS COMMENT IS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT ON PURPOSE - a comment ABOVE <PermissionSet> breaks
        `sf` at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.
        The prose below lived in <description> until 2026-08-31, when a real deploy proved
        PermissionSet.description is capped at 255 characters (measured on usman-dpeg -
        "Description: data value too large: ... (max length=255)") - a DIFFERENT cap from
        CustomField.description (1000, also measured) and LWC .js-meta.xml <description> (255,
        also measured but a separate metadata type). This repo's established pattern for exceeding
        a description cap is to shorten <description> and move the full rationale here.

        Read-only on the Transaction checklist model for personas that VIEW a checklist without
        working it; DPEG_Checklist_Edit is the read/write counterpart. Mirrors the role
        DPEG_TaskChecklist_View plays for the Task-based model.

        Grants NO Wire object or field access at all - wire access stays scoped to the Transaction
        team and admins.

        Includes read on Critical_Date__c.Transaction__c, which stopped being implicitly visible
        when its required flag was relaxed, so assign this wherever DPEG_Transaction_View is
        assigned or that field disappears for those users.
    -->
    <description>Read-only on the Transaction checklist model for personas viewing without working it. No Wire access. See in-file comment for why, including the Critical_Date__c.Transaction__c grant.</description>
